<text x="88.9" y="43.18" size="2.54" layer="100">General IO</text>
<text x="11.43" y="45.72" size="1.27" layer="94">2026, Christian Tambe. Some rights reserved.</text>
<text x="22.86" y="38.1" size="1.27" layer="94">Licensed under a Creative Commons</text>
<text x="22.86" y="35.56" size="1.27" layer="94">Attribution-Share-Alike Unported License.</text>
<text x="22.86" y="33.02" size="1.27" layer="94">See creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/</text>
<text x="22.86" y="86.36" size="1.778" layer="97">Digilent 12-pin Pmod (JA).  Pins 1-4 and 7-10 are signals through 200R series resistors;
pins 5/11 are GND and 6/12 are VCC3V3 -- so a 2x6 header carries EIGHT signals, not twelve,
which is why the names skip JA5/JA6.  No decoupling here: the Pmod spec puts bypassing on the
module, and VCC3V3 already carries ~170uF.  The Cmod A7 has none at its Pmod either.
JA1-JA4 (the top row, the half a Pmod uses for SPI) are all in bank 16: A14 A15 B15 A16.
JA7 is C15, also bank 16.  JA8/JA9/JA10 are W19/N2/W7 -- banks 14/35/34 -- because nothing
else was free.  All five banks are VCCO=3.3V, so this costs timing coherence, not levels.</text>
<text x="10.16" y="308.61" size="1.778" layer="97">X2: 44 pins on a 2.54 mm grid, rows 0.700 in apart, board 69.85 x 20.32 mm.
Numbered right to left and straight through: top row 1-20, bottom row 21-44.
TOP ROW, x 59.69 down to 1.27: GND, +3.3V, GND, then CHAN-CLK and CHAN0..CHAN3
  (pins 4-8), CHAN4 (pin 9), CHAN5..CHAN11 (10-16), +3.3V, +1.8V, +1.0V, GND.
  FOUR positions between pin 9 and pin 10 -- x 36.83, 34.29, 31.75, 29.21 -- are
  RESERVED, not spare: the landing for the edge-mounted micro-USB X1, 7.80 mm of
  copper in 11.176 mm clear, centred with 1.69 mm each side.
BOTTOM ROW, contiguous, x 59.69 down to 1.27: GND, VU, GND, RST#, CHAN12..CHAN28
  (pins 25-41), ANALOG-IO0, ANALOG-IO1, +5V-INPUT.
FIVE grounds: pins 1, 3, 20, 21, 23.  Pin 22 VU SOURCES 5 V, pin 44 only takes it.</text>
</plain>
