<text x="69.85" y="182.88" size="1.778" layer="97">The six pins above CCLK..D03 are the ONLY balls master-SPI configuration can use (UG470).  They are
ordinary user I/O once DONE goes high.  SDRAM A4 moved K19 -&gt; D17 to free FCS_B; the ESP reset
moved D17 -&gt; B15.  microSD is on its own CLK/CMD/DAT0 so a card cannot fight the configuration bus.</text>
<text x="72.39" y="168.91" size="1.778" layer="97">The six microSD signals below CCLK/flash are the native 4-bit SD bus: CLK CMD DAT0-DAT3.
All sit in bank 34 byte group T0 (R2 T1 T2 U1 V2 W2).  DAT1/DAT2 took CHAN1/CHAN0 off the
prototyping header; DAT3 is the old SPI chip-select renamed, so only two pins were spent.</text>
<text x="225.94" y="174.61" size="1.778" layer="97" rot="R180">FT2232H handshake</text>
<text x="97.79" y="245.11" size="5.08" layer="95" rot="R90">CLCK</text>
