<sheet name="FPGA POWER">
<description>FPGA POWER</description>
<plain>
<wire x1="0" y1="0" x2="215.9" y2="0" width="0.3048" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="215.9" y1="0" x2="215.9" y2="279.4" width="0.3048" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="215.9" y1="279.4" x2="0" y2="279.4" width="0.3048" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="0" y1="279.4" x2="0" y2="0" width="0.3048" layer="94"/>
<text x="55.88" y="12.7" size="2.54" layer="100">FPGA POWER</text>
<text x="25.4" y="159.31" size="2.032" layer="97">VCCAUX — 1x47uF, 1x4.7uF, 2x0.47uF</text>
<text x="59.69" y="58.42" size="1.778" layer="97">These three gates are U1 itself -- the same XC7A35T-CPG236 whose I/O are on sheet 6.
VCCO pins are named for the bank they feed (bank 14 has nine supply balls, bank 0 only two).
BANK216 holds the unused transceiver supplies; UG482 requires MGTAVCC/MGTAVTT/MGTRREF
tied to GND when the GTPs are unused.
VCCADC/GNDADC/VREFP/VREFN stay on sheet 6: they sit behind ferrites L6/L7 with C123/C124
as the XADC supply filter, not on these rails.</text>
<text x="133.35" y="218.26" size="1.27" layer="97">BANK 0 VCCO -- 1x47uF (UG483 T2-2)</text>
<text x="153.67" y="192.86" size="1.27" layer="97">BANK 14 VCCO -- 4x0.47uF, 2x4.7uF, 1x47uF (UG483 T2-2)</text>
<text x="148.59" y="170.56" size="1.27" layer="97">BANK 16 VCCO -- 4x0.47uF, 2x4.7uF (UG483 T2-2)</text>
<text x="153.67" y="152.78" size="1.27" layer="97">BANK 34 VCCO -- 4x0.47uF, 2x4.7uF (UG483 T2-2)</text>
<text x="143.51" y="133.72" size="1.27" layer="97">BANK 35 VCCO -- 4x0.47uF, 2x4.7uF (UG483 T2-2)</text>
<text x="66.04" y="211.46" size="1.27" layer="97">VCCINT</text>
<text x="58.42" y="183.52" size="1.27" layer="97">VCCBRAM</text>
<text x="6.35" y="215.87" size="1.27" layer="97">VCCINT -- 3x0.47uF, 1x100uF, 2x4.7uF (UG483 T2-2)</text>
<text x="24.13" y="185.39" size="1.27" layer="97">VCCBRAM -- 1x0.47uF, 1x47uF (UG483 T2-2)</text>
</plain>
